+Handles spatial 1D, 2D, 3D network components with a factory pattern.
+
+A `Factory` is a named registry of callables. Each callable maps a set of arguments (typically the number of
+spatial dimensions) to a layer class. New layer types can be added at runtime without modifying this module:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from monai.networks.layers.factories import Conv
+
+    @Conv.factory_function("myconv")
+    def _my_conv(dim):
+        return MyConvNd[dim - 1]  # some user-defined classes indexed by dim - 1
+
+    layer_cls = Conv.get_constructor("myconv", 2)
+
+The module-level `get_*_type` helpers are kept for backward compatibility and delegate to the factories below.
 """
 
